  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., Example 4 and 5 where prices fell from ~89 to ~77); forecasts consistently overshoot the true low by 10-15 points.",
    "Forecasts fail to capture mean reversion spikes; they predict slow, linear recovery while true outcomes show sharp V-shaped rebounds (e.g., Example 4 and 5 where prices jumped from ~78 to ~96 within 2 weeks).",
    "Sentiment history is largely irrelevant for short-term direction in these examples; the model ignores low sentiment periods that precede sudden price collapses or rallies.",
    "Model assumes monotonic trends based on recent momentum but fails to account for regime shifts, resulting in persistent overestimation during bearish phases and underestimation of volatility.",
    "Apply a downward correction factor of 10-15 points when the last 3 days show a decline >5% and sentiment is neutral or negative."
  ]
}
